{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And charge et Yehoshua.</b> One needs to know what this commandment is, and in Sifrei they said (Pinḥas 136) — and this is its language: \"Charge him concerning the Gibeonites\"; another matter: \"Charge him concerning the disputes,\" and so forth, until here. And this is not explicit in the verse, unless we say that these are words of received tradition. And it is possible to say according to the plain sense of the verse, according to their words, may their memory be for blessing, who said: צַו means nothing other than kingship, as it is written (I Samuel 13:14) ״וַיְצַוֵּהוּ ה׳ לְנָגִיד״ — and see what I explained in the portion of (Exodus 6:13) ״וַיְצַוֵּם אֶל בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״ and so forth. So too, the utterance of HaShem here to Moses comes to mean that in his lifetime Yehoshua shall rule over Israel, and he shall strengthen him in his kingship before the eyes of all Israel."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The Sifrei reference '(פנחס קל״ו)' cites section 136 of Sifrei on Numbers, beginning from parashat Pinchas; the section numbering follows standard editions."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:14:53.482092659Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}